<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Horse breeding</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as horse-breeding</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Horse breeding is the raising of horses for transport, warfare and trade. It underpinned the military power of many empires. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire</a> was renowned for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> horses, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a> depended on steppe herds, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> maintained horses for its cavalry.</p></div>
